(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// Watchers (queue 274; CPython 3.14.10's Objects/dictobject.c, Objects/typeobject.c, Objects/funcobject.c,"] [4 1 "// Objects/codeobject.c and Python/context.c): the core's events the C API's PyDict_AddWatcher, PyType_AddWatcher,"] [5 1 "// PyFunction_AddWatcher, PyCode_AddWatcher and PyContext_AddWatcher deliver. Each hook is nil until the C API"] [6 1 "// (pyctypes) sets it; a dict's and a type's own watcher bits are a field the core checks where it already writes"] [7 1 "// (a dict's version, a type's namespace), so the core pays a nil check, or a byte's, where no watcher is registered."] [8 1 "// The callbacks' errors are the hooks' to report (PyErr_FormatUnraisable): the core's operation goes on."] [10 1 "// The events of PyDict_WatchEvent, PyFunction_WatchEvent, PyCodeEvent and PyContextEvent, CPython's values."] [36 2 "// DictWatch is called before a watched dict (its watcher bits non-zero) changes: _PyDict_NotifyEvent's"] [37 2 "// arguments (CLONED's key the dict copied from; DELETED's value nil)."] [39 2 "// TypeWatch is called when a watched type is modified with its version tag set (type_modified_unlocked)."] [41 2 "// FuncWatch is called when a function is made and when its code, defaults or keyword defaults are set."] [43 2 "// CodeWatch is called when a code object is made (compiled, loaded, unmarshalled, replaced)."] [45 2 "// ContextWatch is called when the current context changes (Context.run's enter and exit): the new current"] [46 2 "// context, nil for none."] [50 1 "// typeWatching is set once a type is watched: from then on lookups and modifications keep the types' version"] [51 1 "// tags (CPython's tp_version_tag, which pyi does not otherwise keep), which aggregate a watched type's events."] [54 1 "// DictWatched and SetDictWatched are a dict's watcher bits (CPython's _ma_watcher_tag's low bits)."] [65 1 "// TypeWatched and SetTypeWatched are a type's watcher bits (tp_watched); watching assigns the version tags"] [66 1 "// (PyType_Watch: the next modification is reported)."] [77 1 "// typeAssignVersion is assign_version_tag: t and its bases' tags set."] [85 1 "// TypeModified is PyType_Modified (the C API's): the watchers told, when a type is watched."] [92 1 "// typeModified is type_modified_unlocked: a type without a version tag is not reported again (its earlier"] [93 1 "// modification already was); its subclasses first, then its own watchers."] [107 1 "// funcCreated reports a function made (PyFunction_EVENT_CREATE)."] [114 1 "// codeCreated reports a code object made (PY_CODE_EVENT_CREATE)."] [121 1 "// contextSwitched reports the thread's current context changed (Py_CONTEXT_SWITCHED)."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis []} (go/file "watchers.go" :imports [])

;; Watchers (queue 274; CPython 3.14.10's Objects/dictobject.c, Objects/typeobject.c, Objects/funcobject.c,
;; Objects/codeobject.c and Python/context.c): the core's events the C API's PyDict_AddWatcher, PyType_AddWatcher,
;; PyFunction_AddWatcher, PyCode_AddWatcher and PyContext_AddWatcher deliver. Each hook is nil until the C API
;; (pyctypes) sets it; a dict's and a type's own watcher bits are a field the core checks where it already writes
;; (a dict's version, a type's namespace), so the core pays a nil check, or a byte's, where no watcher is registered.
;; The callbacks' errors are the hooks' to report (PyErr_FormatUnraisable): the core's operation goes on.


^{:go/pos {:doc [10 1] :lparen [11 7] :rparen [18 1] :tok-pos [11 1]}} (go/const "The events of PyDict_WatchEvent, PyFunction_WatchEvent, PyCodeEvent and PyContextEvent, CPython's values.\n"
